{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791004673,"nonce":"kn5wdib4VebBiXKmFYmOKwWJFxM=","message":"Mac (load ~3, unpinned), same PoolBench, per round of 4 jobs: AOT small 7 us serial / 32-36 pooled, 10x jobs 75 / 67-69; hybrid small 7-8 / 39-44, 10x 280 / 93-112 before 7eb152f and 79 / 78-82 after. Dispatch-and-join overhead ~30-35 us per round on the Mac against ~15-20 on the NUC and ~18 for stock hl there; ~8 us per job is in line with a condvar wake on macOS. The main thread's Lock.wait waits on the scheduler endpoint's condvar (1 ms backstop), no polling. The hybrid 10x row was the leaf-promotion bug 6f575be (fixed 7eb152f), not the pool. Conclusion: no ash-specific dispatch cost; tens-of-microsecond jobs do not pay for a pool on either runtime. What would cut it further is workers spinning briefly before parking, which trades CPU and power for latency.","files":null}]}